## 3.4 Version Information

### Purpose

The Version Information section records the revision history and current approved version of a System Objective.

Its purpose is to preserve engineering history, support traceability across revisions, and clearly identify the current authoritative version of the objective.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following version fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Current Version | Current approved version of the objective (e.g., v1.0). |
| Baseline Version | First approved version of the objective. |
| Version Date | Date the current version became effective. |
| Version Summary | Brief summary of the changes introduced in the current version. |
| Previous Version | Reference to the immediately preceding version, where applicable. |

---

### Version Rules

Version information shall:

- Follow the approved versioning standard.
- Be updated only after formal approval.
- Preserve links to previous approved versions.
- Never overwrite historical version information.

---

### Engineering Note

Version information records the evolution of the objective's engineering content.

The objective's identity remains unchanged regardless of the number of approved versions.
